# Carom

## Overview

Carom is a neon, top-down paddle duel for the browser. Two paddles face each
other across a dark field while a ball ricochets between them, off the top and
bottom walls, and off a pair of obstacles in the middle of the field. A player
scores when the ball passes the far edge behind their opponent's paddle.

Carom's defining mechanic is spin: the motion of a paddle at the moment it
strikes the ball curves the ball's flight afterward. The obstacles turn the open
field into a bank-shot puzzle.

Carom has its own name, look, spin mechanic, and obstacle layout. Do not
reproduce the assets, branding, or design of any existing game.

The specification spans several files under `specs/`. Read all of them and build
the game they describe as one cohesive whole.

